        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "<p>We ended up traveling to London <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.travelzoo.com/collection/vacations/uk/\">on the cheap</a> for Kel's birthday. Because we booked a vacation package, our hotel was in a neighborhood we weren't terribly familiar with called Earl's Court. Lucky for us, Earl's Court is home to the <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.troubadourlondon.com/\">Troubadour</a>, a historic coffee house where Bob Dylan, Paul Simon, Elton John, Morrissey, and <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.troubadourlondon.com/\">many more</a> have all played over the years. Behind the coffee shop is a beautiful, peaceful spot for a stroll called <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/place/Brompton+Cemetery/@51.489714,-0.199073,15z/data=!4m12!1m6!3m5!1s0x48760f8bdf3ada65:0xee14f9e2d887e81d!2sThe+Troubadour!8m2!3d51.4888522!4d-0.1917184!3m4!1s0x0:0xca3562498d604b3f!8m2!3d51.4839686!4d-0.1897207\">Brompton Cemetery</a>. I highly recommend checking them both out!</p>"
    },
